Z||000000||chris6878||06-21-2000||02:47 AM||||My gas mileage sucks...   i am only getting around 15 mpg (V6), and this is highway driving. i filled my tank, drove to work, and filled it again..  it took 5.5 gallons to fill her back up. My trip to work and back is roughly 82 miles.  82 miles/5.5 gal = 14.9     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><BR> So i am roughly getting 15 miles to the gallon. I have recently put on new wires, coil, pickup coil, ign module, and dis cap. I am getting a code 13 last time i checked. Maybe i should go for the Oxygen Sensor next?||||reg||5
Z||000001||Mattsfiero||06-21-2000||02:49 AM||||14.9 miles to the Gallon huh...What are you running for Fuel... I run High Octane and get almost 27Miles to the gallon...Try Upgrading it.....  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> oh and your car will always give you a code 13x3 after that it will give you the problem code<p>[This message has been edited by Mattsfiero (edited 06-21-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||chris6878||06-21-2000||02:52 AM||||boy.. that was a fast respone     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  <P>I run super premium gas always...   my car tends to be hard to start when it gets warmer too... hmm...         <P>thanks for the quick response,<BR>chris   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||14
Z||000003||Oreif||06-21-2000||02:56 AM||||It's code 12 is an ALL OK.<BR>Code 13 is oxygen sensor. I suggest you replace yours. If it isn't working correctly you could be burning too rich hence bad gas mileage. I get about 18/19 city and 26-28 highway. (Of course this all depends on how heavy my right foot is)||||reg||4
Z||000004||tgowens||06-21-2000||02:58 AM||||yeah -- what Matt said! -- only, I run 87 octane in my '87GT stock V-6 and I get 26.9 to 27.8 on the highway -- less in the stop and go city driving........that's with new plugs, wires, dist. cap and roter, O2 sensor, I run synthetic tranny fluid and oil and, oh yes, the engine only has 62,000 miles on it...||||reg||1
Z||000005||Old Lar||06-21-2000||09:31 AM||||My 87 getrag gets 31-33 on the highway.  I use a real light foot the other times.  The milage drops down to mid 20's around town and I use 87 octane.  I had a rebuilt distributor put in last winter, but all else is a few years old.  Since I've owned this car since new, my gas milage has always been good.<P>I suspect driving habits have a lot to do with milage.  I'm not running my car up to 5000-6000 rpm for shift points (unless absolutely necessary).||||reg||3
Z||000006||lennyb4||06-21-2000||09:35 AM||||Thats why i love my duck. I average 27.5 in the city and around 36 on the highway. And i have a slightly heavy foot..  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||6
Z||000007||rogergarrison||06-21-2000||11:21 AM||||my 2 cents:<P>1/ octane dont have anything at all to do with gas milage. All that higher octane does is keep your engine from having detonation......period! So unless you have a 10:1 compression, 87 is plenty.<P>2/ I wish I could get 15 mpg.||||reg||1
Z||000008||Getaway2k||06-22-2000||09:31 PM||||I have an 86 GT with 37000 original miles on it. The best for me in city driving is 18 mpg. I'm not sure about the highway mpg. Due to the price of gas and that kind of gas mileage, I doubt my Fiero will be out of the garage any time soon.||||reg||1
